{:en {:title "Kotoba native performance: Embench progress and pause, 12 October 2026"
:description "All 19 workloads measured: Kotoba currently takes 2.936× C time in geometric mean. Correctness verified; the C-or-faster goal remains unmet and is paused."
:intro "The latest complete 19-workload comparison gives a geometric mean of 2.936× for Kotoba execution time divided by C execution time. C is faster overall. The goal of matching or exceeding C is not achieved; this optimization campaign is paused as of 12 October 2026."
:notice "These are exploratory measurements of translated Kotoba programs using the upstream Embench speed driver and formula. They are not a certified official Kotoba Embench score, a released-toolchain result, or a claim of speed on other hosts."
:sections [{:title "How to read the numbers"
:paragraphs ["1.000× means equal execution time. Above 1.000× means Kotoba takes longer and C is faster; below 1.000× means Kotoba is faster. The total is the geometric mean across all 19 workloads, not the arithmetic mean. CRC32 is the one workload with a ratio below one in this cycle."]
