{:title "What was verified"
:paragraphs ["The adopted native compiler is local source commit fc49cb2ee6fea1a41a5abbc8ed5b52aaa9f19471. It is not integrated into main or published as a release. This result does not describe the released CLI."
"The original 19 workloads and 95 profile cases were preserved. Qualification covered 39 native images and 483 paired comparisons, including fuel boundaries and interaction cases. Original results, state and resource accounting were checked. Compiler self-hosting and additional generic controls were also verified. Correctness qualification alone does not establish performance."]}
{:title "Measurement method and limits"
:paragraphs ["Both arms were timed on the same macOS arm64 host; the C arm uses Apple clang 17.0.0. Upstream Embench revision 09c2ed8c3b7008c95d08b038de4a3f6dc103ed70 supplies the untouched speed driver and score formula. The C executables were previously frozen and freshly timed in this cycle."
"Kotoba uses GSF 8192 and C uses GSF 32768. The driver normalizes each arm by its declared global scale factor. The ratio is C relative-speed score divided by Kotoba relative-speed score: 37345.764989 / 12718.199531 = 2.936403. These raw scores are host-specific and are not scores per MHz."
"CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW brackets the workload body. One warmup body, resets and verification occur outside that interval; representation allocation inside the body remains timed. Each language has one accepted sample per workload. CPU admission requires at least 70% raw idle before and during timing, plus 70% background idle during timing. CPU-only retries retain all attempts and select the first admitted sample, not the fastest."
"This is one exploratory measurement cycle without a statistical confidence claim. Translated-port representation and execution paths differ from original C; using the official driver and formula does not turn the Kotoba port into a certified, unmodified official submission. Historical partial measurements are excluded from this total."]}
{:title "Changes adopted locally"
:paragraphs ["The current compiler combines optimizations for masked XOR, private literal-width calls, forwarding call results into comparisons, repeated stack loads after disjoint scalar stores, signed division by two, and reuse of successful cached vector bounds checks. Each adopted change retained the required correctness and ABI checks."
"There is no minimum improvement percentage cutoff. Even small validated improvements can accumulate. For example, a prior picojpeg change with an observed 0.085% reduction was adopted locally; that small-sample observation is not a statistically established effect. Per-change observations come from different runs and must not be added into a total speedup."]}
{:title "Work preserved at the pause"
:paragraphs ["Descriptor-bounds witness reuse and conditional-fallthrough vector-view reuse each passed the full 39-image and 483-comparison correctness checks against the adopted baseline. They remain unadopted: additional generic or semantic controls, performance measurements and adoption review are pending. Their candidate results are excluded from the measured table."
"The statemate timing files were transferred and custody checked, but the timing campaign was not started. A bounded byte-lookup candidate remains a source prototype, with compiler execution and runtime qualification still pending."
"Optimization agents and the C-or-faster goal have been paused. Evidence, worktrees and unfinished candidates are retained for a deliberate future restart. No performance goal completion is claimed."]}]
